Z||000000||Rex||11-24-2001||09:30 PM||||just wondering could some tell me if a 2m4 means a 4-cyl engine? my car has the 2.8 and seems to be unaltered.sticker is on right rear on engine deck lid.....thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||K2m4||11-24-2001||09:35 PM||||something is amiss then, maybe the trunk lid was replaced at one point, but yes 2M4 means 4 cyl and 2M6 means 6<P>Kerm<BR>86 GT<BR>86 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brandon86SE||11-24-2001||09:35 PM||||That's very odd since 2M4 means 2-seater, Mid engined, 4-cylinder, and 2M6 is for the 6-cylinder......  Someone put the wrong sticker on it?  Or else an engine swap.  Hard to say.<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||11-24-2001||09:37 PM||||2: two seater<BR>M: mid engine<BR>4: 4-cyl<BR>6: 6-cyl<P>If it says 2M4 then someone probably installed a "new" decklid.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Devotshka||11-24-2001||09:38 PM||||Check the VIN... i think the 8th digit is the engine ID, 9 should be V6.  I'm not sure what the 4cyl is, but if yer VIN says 9, then you got a replacement decklid (or someone used the wrong sticker), if otherwise, its had an engine transplant.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||11-24-2001||09:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Devotshka:<BR><B>Check the VIN... i think the 8th digit is the engine ID, 9 should be V6.  I'm not sure what the 4cyl is, but if yer VIN says 9, then you got a replacement decklid (or someone used the wrong sticker), if otherwise, its had an engine transplant.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 4-cyl. VIN code is "R". ||||reg||1
